The Maestro does not automatically consume every available signal.
Information remains subject to authorization, necessity, purpose, privacy, and applicable policy.
Resonance is therefore selective.
The existence of context does not imply permission to use it.
The existence of memory does not imply that it should be activated.
The existence of a capability does not imply that it should be executed.
The existence of a provider does not imply that it should receive information.
The existence of an action does not imply that the human authorized it.
The Maestro must preserve these distinctions.
Maestro Resonance coordinates intent across the ecosystem.
